/// the cheap call also requires every member to return the identical type.
///
/// `{closed_target}` selects the commonest route, a single non-generic Vize
/// SFC, before the factory is built. That route is the factory's marked
/// constructor member, `(component: unknown) => <A>(props: $EmitInput<…>) =>
/// __EmitProps<$UnionEmit<C>>`, and its return never reads `A`. For one
/// member (identical to the whole type, so no union), `$UnionEmit<C>` is the
/// `$emit` the closed check infers, and `{closed_factory}`, `(component:
/// unknown) => (props: any) => __EmitProps<E>`, is the same factory minus its
/// props input. `__vize_emit_input` then returns that call unchanged: its own
/// branches would make the same `(props: any) => R` of it, and the full
/// factory's single signature returns the same `R` where they would not.
/// Unions, `any`, `never`, generic resolvers, unmarked constructors and an
/// `$emit` of `never` keep the full factory and the full gate.
